		)
		)
	)
	(text_box "WHY A 1:4 TREE AND NOT ONE GATE.  One 74LVC1G34 driving fourteen flip-flop inputs plus their traces is about 100 pF, which gives 5-8 ns edges.  Per-flip-flop clock threshold mismatch converts to skew\nas dV/slew, so a slow edge multiplies a 5 mV threshold difference into 12 ps instead of 3 ps.  Two stages keep every branch at 1-2 ns.  33R at each driver is series termination: at a 1 ns edge the\nbranch is a transmission line once it is longer than about 45 mm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.2400 345.4400 0)
